  "description": "Logs application events into a SQL database\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n      Create this table in your SQL database:\n\n      CREATE TABLE Logs (\n      Id INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY,\n      Timestamp DATETIME,\n      LogLevel NVARCHAR(50),\n      Category NVARCHAR(100),\n      Message NVARCHAR(MAX),\n      Exception NVARCHAR(MAX) null\n      );\n\n      Use It in a .NET App\n\n      using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\n      using AKS.Sql.Logger;\n\n\n      AKSSqlLogger aKSSqlLogger = new AKSSqlLogger(categoryName, \"Server=<Server_Name></Server_Name>;Database=<DBNAME></DBNAME>;Trusted_Connection=True;TrustServerCertificate=True;\");\n\n      try\n      {\n\n      aKSSqlLogger.Log(LogLevel.Information, \"Record is saved successfully\");\n\n      }\n      catch (Exception ex)\n      {\n      aKSSqlLogger.LogException(LogLevel.Error, ex);\n\n      }\n\n      This version exposes two method. one to capture Log and another to capture Exception.  Easy to use in .net app.",
